# Belt and braces: the Dockerfile copies named paths rather than the whole tree, so nothing here
# is load-bearing on its own. It matters for what reaches the build context at all -- anything
# sent there can end up in an intermediate layer or a cache export, so the two secrets are
# excluded here as well as never being copied.

certs/
config/local*.json
.env

node_modules/
logs/
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
test/
docs/
# ...except the one XSD the shipped config/specializations.manifest.json points at. The Dockerfile
# copies it so that `node scripts/build-specializations.js` runs inside the image against the
# manifest as shipped. A later pattern wins over an earlier one, so this line has to stay below
# `docs/`.
!docs/examples/specializations/parkingBlock.xsd
*.md
.claude/
.superpowers/
.nvmrc
ecosystem.config.js
